let me introduce at this time our two  senior speakers Morgan Delp is a senior  with a 3.5 5 grade point average her  major is history of a minor his  journalism Oregon intends to pursue a  career as a writer at Hillsdale she  belongs to the Catholic society and the  Kappa Kappa Gamma sorority she  volunteers for the king's covered  project and the Hillsdale buddy project  and serves on the student athletic  Advisory Committee she also helps with  the campus newspaper that's an  understatement she's the editor of the  campus newspaper this year she  participates in the journalism program  and plays on the women's tennis team to  cover to help cover her college expenses  she works as a student affairs mentor as  well I teased Morgan before the ceremony  that I was going to add that she also  takes classes Morgan is the oldest of  five children  her sister Sydney attends Hillsdale the  family resides in Holland Ohio and her  father is the chairman and chief  executive officer of the TBC thank you  dr. Whalen  good afternoon hell's Dell College class  of 2018 parents students faculty staff  and guests I am truly honored to be able  to speak to you all today it's hard to  believe that three years ago I sat where  you are sitting it's even harder to  believe that my sister Sydney is sitting  among you as a mentor and her third year  here and that my little brother Dugan is  sitting out there as a freshman a part  of me wants to use this time to  embarrass him in front of his future  classmates since he is so smart and  clever that it's usually him poking fun  at me but I will spare him that  humiliation and you all the family  stories when it was time to say goodbye  to my family like you will do soon I  turned to face my dad whose eyes were  welling up with tears I couldn't believe  my strong optimistic dad was crying at  my departure starting to become  emotional myself and preparing words of  encouragement in my head I embraced him  and a hug I expected some hurtful  heartfelt words from dear old dad  as his firstborn left home for the first  time but instead he said I wish I was  going to college while lacking  appropriate fatherly sentiment my dad at  Hillsdale graduate summed up in that act  how special and happy of a place  Hillsdale was for him while a lot of  things have changed around here since he  graduated in 1986 the happiness of its  students has not recently the  prestigious Princeton Review ranked  Hillsdale 10th and happiest students of  all colleges in the country the reason  it's the people seeing on is a sign seen  on a sign as you enter Hillsdale this  well-worn motto reflects the  friendliness and quirkiness of the  town's 8,000 or so citizens although it  has almost become a cliche around here  it's a fitting summation for the college  as well  we are all here because we believe in  higher things like beauty truth and  goodness even if you haven't learned  exactly how to express them yet we want  to become better thinkers better people  it is happy to be around others who  value these things at a certain level it  starts with a faculty and staff they  truly care about us students my  professors have had my classmates and me  to their homes for dinner multiple times  I've given tennis lessons to my  professors children people invite their  teachers to their weddings I have  attended a wedding of two students that  was held at a professor's house just the  other morning Steve Cassie who greets  everyone as they enter the North family  dining room made it a point to show me a  picture of myself playing tennis in one  of the recent Hillsdale mailings the  kindness of those that lead our school  trickles down to and throughout the rest  of campus homer in the odyssey a book  you freshmen will all read said for a  friend with an understanding heart is  worth no less than a brother homer is  right and you will make those family  like friends here at Hillsdale it's a  hard school an understanding will come  in handy from your roommate when in a  couple weeks you receive  your first ever see and cry on the phone  to your mom for an hour but that  understanding friend will also be there  to celebrate your first a which you  achieve only after hundreds of combined  library and office hours some of your  best memories will be staying up until  2:00 a.m. in the Suites little computer  room writing a Western religion essay  with four of your Hall mates or bonding  in the library with someone unexpected  while trying to understand the physics  of Isaac Newton for physical science  class you'll look back and remember the  van rides to the Upper Peninsula with  your tennis team the president's balls  with your sorority sisters the welcome  parties with friends the late nights in  the collegian office with your fellow  editors at least these are the things I  know I will remember there's something  more than just our shared age group and  approximate location that drew us into  these friendships with one another  it's that truth that our real school  motto tells us we pursue as expressed in  our honor code every other student here  has signed and agreed to this code like  you have sure we will fail to live up to  that at times but we attend to school  where others hold you accountable for  your actions being honorable dutiful and  respectful as that code states is  important the best examples of this Duty  and the kindness of the people on this  campus can be summed up in two  embarrassing experiences I had my  freshman year which may serve to ease  your nerves the first time you show up  late to class or trip walking up the  dorm stairs one evening while eating  dinner in the dining hall by myself I  made myself a bowl of the granola cereal  I devoured it but within minutes I could  feel my throat swelling I'm allergic to  one of the nuts in the mix and being the  fopen freshman I was didn't think to ask  any of the employees what the mix  contained I sprinted to the back office  where two students who saw me panicking  followed quickly behind the food staff  went to work on calling 9-1-1 and  getting me help one of the students a  close friend stayed with me to keep me  calm while the other a girl I barely  knew sprinted to my dorm room to  retrieve my epi  I lucked out because she was a  nationally ranked swimmer who was also  very fast on land I recovered quickly  after a trip to the ER where my friends  stayed with me the entire time you think  I would have learned my lesson at that  point but only weeks later I suffered a  similar reaction in a JS cafe this time  by the ice cream God was watching over  me again because as my throat started to  swell and I slunk down lower in my AJ's  booth two girls noticed my concern and  marched me to the bathroom this time I  had my EpiPen I will never forget how  the one let me squeeze her hand until it  turned blue as I injected myself with  the pen and how the other drove me to  the Hillsdale hospital and that year's  first snowstorm driving about 15 miles  per hour the entire way while I hope all  of you do not have to learn the  greatness of hills dales people in this  embarrassing and dangerous way I do hope  you do experience it what's more I hope  you become these people to others be the  people that seek the best in themselves  and others be the ones that uphold our  honor code via the people that think for  themselves practice individual  responsibilities and work hard if you  embrace the next four years and beyond  in such a way it may be you sitting out  there 25 years from now tearing up as  you say goodbye to your daughter on her  first day of college remembering them  people that made Hillsdale College so  special  you
 

